WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.620
In order for a phoenix to be reborn, it first
has to die.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.980
And that's what Dark Phoenix is essentially
about: the death of the X-Men franchise at

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.740
Fox, so it may be gloriously reborn at Marvel
Studios.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.540
But, wow, do we have some questions!

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:16.120
Here's a spoiler-filled look at the biggest
unanswered questions in Dark Phoenix.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:21.300
At the beginning of Dark Phoenix, the X-Men
go on a mission to save some astronauts menaced

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.540
by a weird space cloud.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.400
"he is here."

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.880
No, not that weird space cloud.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.680
Not that one either.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.860
This is a totally different space cloud that
turns out to be the Phoenix Force.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.450
And then bad things happen for two hours.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.070
But that raises a big question: didn't Jean
already have the Phoenix Force?

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.600
Like, just in the last movie?

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.200
"unleash your power!

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.400
Let go, Jean!

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.120
Jean, let go!"

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.740
X-Men: Apocalypse was set in 1983, a full
nine years before the events of Dark Phoenix.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:07.160
So if she just got the Phoenix Force now,
what the heck was that all about?

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:12.120
At the climax of the film, the U.S. government
decides to crack down on mutants, rounding

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.120
up all the X-Men in a campaign to imprison
mutants in concentration camps.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.240
The X-Men break free in a massive battle.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:19.220
But then what?

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:23.100
Yes, somehow after violently destroying a
government train and leveling the countryside,

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:27.730
at the cost of numerous U.S. military lives,
the X-Men are then shown being totally fine

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:28.560
back at school.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:29.620
So what happened?

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:33.680
And what about all the other mutants in America,
like the refugees on Magneto's island?

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.820
Are they all still huddling in a mutant camp
somewhere under armed guard?

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:38.900
Out of sight, out of mind, apparently.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.620
Remember X-Men: Days of Future Past?

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:46.070
In that film, the future turned to hot poop,
so the cast from the original X-Men trilogy

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:49.950
sent Hugh Jackman into the prequel trilogy
to create a new timeline where the future

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:50.520
was nice.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.740
It sort of worked.

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.260
He saved his Jean Grey… but apparently doomed
this other version, because now the prequels

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.979
aren't prequels anymore, they're a totally
different timeline.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.120
It's a timeline where time itself doesn't
seem to work anymore.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.900
Remember that X-Men: First Class was set way
back in 1963.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:10.671
That means that characters like Magneto, Xavier,
and Mystique should all be in their 50s or

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:14.260
early 60s by the time Dark Phoenix comes around
in 1992.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.300
And yet, they don't seem to have aged a day
in 30 years.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.500
Even characters like Storm and Cyclops who
first appeared in Apocalypse, are still the

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.500
exact same age nine years later.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:29.280
Between the original X-Men films, these not-actually-prequels,
whatever Days of Future Past was, and Logan,

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.800
there seem to be four distinct X-Men timelines.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.880
So congrats!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.180
The movies are finally as confusing as the
comics.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.140
A lot has been written about the end of Dark
Phoenix, which reportedly was totally changed

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.720
at the last minute because the original ending
was way too similar to Captain Marvel.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:47.851
And the haste shows, because the big battle
on the train leaves a lot of questions, the

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.940
main one being: What happened to all the aliens
Jean didn't kill?

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.940
These aliens seemed to be nearly invulnerable,
shrugging off bullets and mutant attacks with

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.440
ease.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.460
But, like, two dozen of them are simply knocked
off the train by optic blasts from Cyclops,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.340
or a strong wind from Storm.

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:05.340
Given how tough they are, it seems likely
that most of those aliens survived a simple

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:05.840
fall.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:06.980
So what happened with them?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:07.940
Are they still on Earth?

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.140
Did they get back on their missing spaceship
and fly away?

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.610
And is anyone ever going to comment on the
fact that there are ALIENS on Earth?

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:14.610
Guess we'll never know!

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:18.080
Speaking of Days of Future Past, remember
this?

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.600
"they told me you can control metal."

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:20.980
"they?"

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.440
"you know, my mom once knew a guy who could
do that.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.660
And what about this bit from Apocalypse?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:30.680
"I'm your…

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.560
I'm here for my family too."

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.680
Yes, the fact that Quicksilver is secretly
Magneto's son is a major subplot.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:46.680
In fact, it's the only character development
for Quicksilver in all three films combined.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.640
So we have to ask: Did they ever have that
dang talk?

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.180
Unfortunately, we don't know, because Quicksilver
disappears from Dark Phoenix less than halfway

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:54.680
through it.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.220
Magneto, meanwhile, heads off to Europe to
check out the amateur chess scene.

00:03:58.239 --> 00:04:02.090
And since this is likely the last time we'll
see these versions of the characters, it seems

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:04.460
we'll never find out whether they ever got
closure.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.160
One thing is certain, though: the viewers
definitely didn't!

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:12.620
After the final credits roll on Dark Phoenix,
the first question many X-Men fans have is:

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:13.800
Why was this movie made?

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:15.220
We're not being snarky.

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:19.799
We're just wondering why, with over 55 years
of great X-Men stories to choose from, Fox

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.960
decided to tell the Dark Phoenix story twice
in seven films.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:28.080
Especially considering 2006's The Last Stand
is considered the worst X-Men film of them

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:28.580
all.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.160
Well… it was until now, anyway!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:34.800
The fact is that there are so many superhero
films in theaters these days that fans want

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:35.880
and need to see something new.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.780
Why they didn't get something new here is
a question we may never get an answer to.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:44.520
Finally, the biggest unanswered question of
them all is simply: now what?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.080
Technically, there's still one more X-Men
film coming from Fox the horror-tinged spinoff

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:53.279
New Mutants, which has been delayed and pushed
back on the schedule repeatedly, and which

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.280
is currently set to debut on April 3, 2020.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.940
After that, though, it's just a matter of
time before Marvel Studios does something

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.620
with the X-Men.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:04.720
Thanks to their deal with Fox, Marvel Studios
films couldn't even mention the whole concept

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:08.059
of mutants, so we're not sure how they'll
bring the X-Men into the mix.

00:05:08.059 --> 00:05:11.879
And it's also likely that Marvel will want
to completely recast the characters, meaning

00:05:11.879 --> 00:05:15.810
fans might be meeting their third Jean Grey
and their third Storm in as many decades.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:20.029
It's a big ask for the audience, though Marvel
proved with Tom Holland and Spider-Man that

00:05:20.029 --> 00:05:20.920
they can make it work.

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.300
The ashes are here.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.700
We're just waiting to see how the resurrection
goes.

